abel":"text","orig":"may not be required if an acid such as an acrylic acid is used as a monomer in the system.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":719.3333333333334,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":83.33333333333333,"r":510.6666666666667,"t":755.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,90],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"may not be required if an acid such as an acrylic acid is used as a monomer in the system."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Dynamic light scattering (DLS) of latex particles","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":678.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":84.66666666666667,"r":359.6666666666667,"t":696.0},"charspan":[0,49],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"Dynamic light scattering (DLS) of latex particles"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"PNIPAM latex particles samples were prepared with varying concentrations of crosslinker (ie N,N'-methylenebis(acrylamide) (BIS)) and surfactant (i.e. A summary of the composition present   (wt% based on the monomer   latex particles)  in the samples and their in Table below. The Z-average particle size (DLS Z-Ave) and polydispersity index (PDI) results of the latex particles obtained from DLS experiments are also provided in Table 1 . To test for reversibility in temperature response; the measurements were first taken at (i) a temperature of about 40*C, then at (ii) a temperature of about 20'C and finally (iii) at a temperature of about 40'C. As shown in Table 1, the average particle size recorded at temperature (iii) for the   samples remains relatively similar to those recorded at temperature   (i) Therefore; the temperature response was proven to be reversible.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":389.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":83.33333333333333,"r":512.6666666666666,"t":653.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,876],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"PNIPAM latex particles samples were prepared with varying concentrations of crosslinker (ie N,N'-methylenebis(acrylamide) (BIS)) and surfactant (i.e. A summary of the composition present   (wt% based on the monomer   latex particles)  in the samples and their in Table below. The Z-average particle size (DLS Z-Ave) and polydispersity index (PDI) results of the latex particles obtained from DLS experiments are also provided in Table 1 . To test for reversibility in temperature response; the measurements were first taken at (i) a temperature of about 40*C, then at (ii) a temperature of about 20'C and finally (iii) at a temperature of about 40'C. As shown in Table 1, the average particle size recorded at temperature (iii) for the   samples remains relatively similar to those recorded at temperature   (i) Therefore; the temperature response was proven to be reversible."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Table 1. Summary of composition and DLS results of PNIPAM samples synthesized for hetero-coagulation studies","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":326.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":83.66666666666667,"r":463.3333333333333,"t":363.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,108],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"Table 1. Summary of composition and DLS results of PNIPAM samples synthesized for hetero-coagulation studies"}],"version":"1.10.0"}